  "course_description": "Support learning in statistics and data science courses by working directly with instructors and students. Develop skills in organization, communication, and mentorship. Must apply and be approved for a specific position in the preceding semester; permission required.",
  "course_notes": "Undergraduate Teaching Assistants (UTAs) and Learning Assistants (LAs) for DATASCI 100. Instructor permission required. Students must submit the application form before receiving permission. Apply at: https://forms.office.com/r/Xn8zvWy8pQ. DATASCI 100 Undergraduate Teaching Assistant (UTA) and Learning Assistant (LA) Positions: We are seeking motivated students who have successfully completed DATASCI 100 to serve as peer mentors. Preference is given to those pursuing the Data Science minor. While completion of QTM 150 and QTM 200 is not required, it is strongly recommended. All UTAs must be available to attend Friday labs in person, and all LAs must be available to lead weekly review sessions on weekends. UTAs will be enrolled in 1 credit, while LAs will be enrolled in 2 credits.",
